-82ba-4021-865f-6ad96b94ba21","position":{"commit_sha":"d10fcc651a663974de4ebe2b35571fa069efe8f8","position":"1787417748370301001-8bfec4de-82ba-4021-865f-6ad96b94ba21"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase-5 residual-gap disposition sweep (RP-06, before epic close):\n\n1. Bedrock completion-banking flake (test_completion_banking_behavior_0707) surfaced by S7's AC7 live matrix — FILED as bug airworthy-topaz-redpoll (88b8-5808-23c0-48c5), linked discovered_from this epic. Pre-existing, bedrock-only, unrelated to RP-06.\n2. Repo-fsck flake (bug de95-1594-1056-436e) — FILED (earlier this run).\n3. AC7 attestation-laundering (the operator-attested criterion cited an exact repo path) — FIXED IN SCOPE on bc13: split into an untagged code-verifiable canary criterion (verified by the completion gate) + an operator-attested external-run-outcome criterion; provenance enum corrected to privilege_posture=production-equivalent / instrument=live-call; re-reviewed (PASS) and re-certified before close.\n4. S7 LLM-Review advisory #2 (_merge_mismatches dedup ordering, cosmetic) — ACCEPTED: output is a set-semantics report; ordering is not contract.\n5. bc13 P6 ac-quality advisory (some AC lines bundle deliverables with 'and') — ACCEPTED: the ACs are the epic-authored contract; further splitting is cosmetic and would re-stale the signed attestation; non-blocking.\n6. S7 surface-parity census — MCP/API slot ACCEPTED out-of-scope per plan: effective-policy discovery is a library/CLI-internal review-kernel concern with no MCP tool surface; the code-review/plan-review library facades ARE exercised (canary + unit matrix).\n7. S5 self-implement deviation — ACCEPTED (recorded on df80 during S5).\n\nNo undisposed enumerated gaps remain.","timestamp":1787416037670516001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787080843858834001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d15a2453-71a8-434f-bbf3-fb467ce8b56f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"},{"link_uuid":"c34d11e4-fc51-4cb5-8a1e-8d79e6c70e67","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"10c8-9981-3877-4ed5"},{"link_uuid":"e597e510-e7bd-4125-a81b-fd2e7c978e3a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75"},{"link_uuid":"ec98f4ea-07bc-4d15-8531-88d17492a8f1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"955f-4b76-59bb-4bf0"},{"link_uuid":"b06e80a5-ce0d-43b3-809a-5adda1070743","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4ae1-ecf8-3aa8-4993"},{"link_uuid":"5432edfd-e6f0-4dca-9e85-ae13475fd6a2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7e0d-7815-4425-4fdb"},{"link_uuid":"fda8a96d-79e1-4cf2-8956-51176e5a987e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4144-2784-6437-4efb"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nPlan review and code review currently make discovery decisions through partially independent registry, routing, runner, checkpoint, and failure paths. This lets one review schedule disabled built-ins, omit activated project DET criteria, ignore project applicability or an authored budget, and mistake failed work for a successful checkpoint. The recovered RP-06 design and the completed research on `rubellite-secondary-cub` establish that these are policy-ownership defects, not merely duplicated code.\n\nThe durable intent sources are session log `supporting-chummy-snake`, recovery ticket `irascible-clueless-basenji`, and the approved decisions recorded on `rubellite-secondary-cub`. RP-01 remains authoritative for request-local provider retry, context, output-size, and structured-output behavior; this epic does not create another provider retry loop or truncate authoritative review input.\n\n## Outcome and Architecture\nImplement one review-discovery architecture:\n\n`CriteriaSnapshot -> gate-owned strategy -> DiscoveryStagePlan -> shared executor -> DiscoveryStageResult -> gate-owned verdict policy`\n\nOne immutable repository-bound effective-policy snapshot includes built-ins, project LLM criteria, project DET criteria, routing, prompts, posture, applicability, and a digest. Gate strategies retain their own context and topology rules. The shared executor owns typed unit outcomes, usage, budget enforcement, cancellation, and success-only checkpoint mechanics; it does not choose applicability, truncate inputs, retry provider turns, or decide a gate verdict.\n\nThe final failure policy continues independent work after RP-01 exhausts a local operation, retains successful findings, skips dependency-blocked work with provenance, and returns unsigned `INDETERMINATE` when blocking-capable coverage is missing unless a real blocking finding takes precedence. Advisory-only gaps may still pass. Systemic configuration, cancellation, deterministic-floor, and whole-tier failure behavior remains fail-safe.\n\n## Required Behavior\n- Project code-review LLM criteria require a non-empty list of non-empty repository-relative globs; `[\"**\"]` means repository-wide. Migrate `project.review-phase-boundaries` from `[]` to `[\"**\"]` without changing its current membership, and as part of that migration audit and update any documentation, examples, or config references that cite the old empty-list (`[]`) glob semantics so none remain stale after the explicit-repository-wide convention lands.\n- Built-in criteria retain their established secondary-trigger semantics, project DET remains detector-selected, and plan-review project criteria retain `applies_at` and `trigger` semantics.\n- Positive explicit `usd_budget` values are authoritative on both gates. For code review, omission is uncapped. For plan review, omission preserves the existing plan-review budget policy: the current authored/default per-review budget cap continues to apply (omission is not uncapped for plan review), so this epic changes no plan-review budget-omission behavior. On both gates zero remains invalid and never acts as a disable switch.\n- Preserve code review sequential execution, no code-review checkpoints, base-reviewer payloads, one-hop Round B, and authored YAML/BPMN topology.\n- Preserve plan review chunking, concurrency, cache warming, checkpointing, container/prerequisite stages, and cancellation behavior while moving to a new digest-complete success-only checkpoint namespace. Legacy checkpoints never seed the new path.\n- Persist a versioned typed discovery trace for retry, audit, and diagnostics. Review and review-status responses remain narrow end-result contracts and do not expose per-unit debugging detail, raw prompts, ticket content, provider payloads, or secrets.\n- Add `rebar review-plan --retry`: only the literal latest completed `INDETERMINATE` review with retryable missing calls is eligible; reuse content-identical successes, retry only missing calls, and grant each explicit retry a fresh attempt budget. Changed or unreadable lineage refuses with zero calls. `--retry` is incompatible with `--force`, `--status`, and `--check`, while `--no-sign` remains compatible.\n- Document `--retry` in canonical CLI help, generated command reference, the user guide, the plan-review gate guide, and exit-code guidance.\n- The workflow editor shows editable Authored Workflow separately from read-only Effective Policy.\n\n## Migration and Rollback\nUse expand-contract without duplicate model calls: compute the legacy and new deterministic projections from the same observed calls, compare selection/order/context/model/budget/posture/usage/checkpoint decisions, and allow only approved deltas. Keep the legacy projection non-default during the compatibility window so a code revert can restore it; do not add an operator configuration flag solely for rollback. New code ignores legacy checkpoint envelopes, and old code ignores the new namespace.\n\n## Testing\nEach child begins with the smallest RED oracle that crosses its real seam: in-process policy and executor tests, real producer-to-consumer contract tests for journals and verdicts, real CLI subprocess tests for `--retry`, workflow-editor tests for authored/effective separation, and a final live review exercise because this epic cuts over production LLM paths. Stateful fault tests assert exact partial results, collateral state, and clean retry behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Both review gates derive selection from one immutable effective-policy snapshot, including effective built-in retunes/disables and activated project LLM/DET criteria.\n- [x] The shared discovery executor emits typed success, resumed, skipped, shed, failed, and cancelled outcomes; only success/resumed outcomes can seed the new checkpoint namespace.\n- [x] Code review preserves its scheduler, base-reviewer, topology, and narrow response contracts while enforcing approved applicability, budget, and partial-failure behavior.\n- [x] Plan review preserves its scheduler, cache, topology, and narrow response contracts while using digest-complete journals and approved partial-failure behavior.\n- [x] `rebar review-plan --retry` reuses eligible successes, retries only missing work with a fresh budget, refuses all stale/ineligible lineages before any model call, and is documented on every canonical operator surface.\n- [x] The workflow editor separates editable Authored Workflow from read-only Effective Policy and rejects an empty project code-review LLM glob list with the `[\"**\"]` remedy.\n- [x] Cross-gate shadow traces show only approved behavior deltas, and a live end-to-end exercise proves the defaulted discovery paths against a real supported provider before the epic closes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","4144-2784-6437-4efb"],["relates_to","4ae1-ecf8-3aa8-4993"],["relates_to","7e0d-7815-4425-4fdb"],["relates_to","955f-4b76-59bb-4bf0"],["relates_to","9b75-8bb5-601d-402d"],["relates_to","ee98-a2c0-7d12-4c75"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Container epic; implementation paths are declared on its seven child stories.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"04075791-d644-4b19-ab4d-44ce788d8d4f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["janitor","rp-06","llm","architecture"],"ticket_id":"58bd-d656-c52f-4cf4","ticket_type":"epic","title":"RP-06 — Unified effective-policy discovery for review gates","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b06e80a5-ce0d-43b3-809a-5adda1070743","4521b324-c18f-4147-8209-77f734666e08","2e1df59c-931b-4541-9e81-b4b690039e13","43a986ab-6f48-4fe7-a06c-89aaec296251","a6d8983a-7aa9-4a1c-b27a-26a646a1de47","5432edfd-e6f0-4dca-9e85-ae13475fd6a2","fda8a96d-79e1-4cf2-8956-51176e5a987e","838b8371-325f-49bb-af4f-8fd1af78ecd4","63b6fa77-d5df-4609-9a52-0b194d644138","f9c8adc2-a3f9-4f68-b79d-1950e9078f72","04075791-d644-4b19-ab4d-44ce788d8d4f","8bfec4de-82ba-4021-865f-6ad96b94ba21"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787421916976402206,"uuid":"c0d61df3-2ab3-4224-9af1-4e4db7c3c28c"}